abugida — notice on what the dedication covers

The code and the documentation of this repository are dedicated to the
public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal (see LICENSE). The dedication covers
them and nothing else.

Some evaluation scripts in eval/ read case files extracted from works that
are not this project's to license:

  - Thomas Oberlies, "Pali: A Grammar of the Language of the Theravada
    Tipitaka" (De Gruyter) — word pairs read from its phonology chapter
    (eval/oberlies.py, eval/oberlies_attested.py, eval/validation/);
  - Wilhelm Geiger, "A Pali Grammar", tr. B. Ghosh, rev. K. R. Norman
    (Pali Text Society) — word pairs harvested from an OCR of it
    (eval/geiger.py);
  - the Digital Pali Dictionary (https://github.com/digitalpalidictionary/dpd-db),
    under its own licence — variant pairs from dpd_headwords.var_phonetic
    (eval/hard_battery.py) and the lexicon several scripts query.

None of these files, and none of the books, is in this repository or in any
distribution of the package. Each user keeps a local copy in eval/data/
(ignored by git) or in the directory named by ABUGIDA_EVAL_DATA, made from
their own copy of the source where a script can make it (--harvest). A
script whose case file is missing says so and exits without error.

References to sections of those grammars (e.g. "Oberlies §15.1") and the
individual Pali and Sanskrit word forms cited as examples in the code and
documentation are citations of facts about the language, not reproductions
of the works.
